commit e57e08fed8f202e9b4e33bb4da9afb1c3cd41638
Author: TarimoPaul <chiefmaster7066@gmail>
Date:   Mon Oct 19 19:29:08 2026 +0300

    GL: reverse() takes the per-entry advisory lock and re-checks under it
    
    Two reversals of the same entry at the same moment (reopen + supersede, a double
    click) both passed their callers' "already reversed?" check, which runs outside the
    reversal's transaction, and wrote two reversals. reverse() now takes
    pg_advisory_xact_lock(hashtext(originalEntryUid)) first and returns without writing
    when a live reversal already exists.
    
    GlConcurrentPostCheck (real PostgreSQL, -Dgl.lock.check=true): 25/25 rounds of two
    simultaneous reversals leave one reversal (without the lock: 25/25 left two).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/com/Lsms/CapitalAndExpenditure/gl/PostingEngine.java b/src/main/java/com/Lsms/CapitalAndExpenditure/gl/PostingEngine.java
index 287e4f5..3f2007d 100644
--- a/src/main/java/com/Lsms/CapitalAndExpenditure/gl/PostingEngine.java
+++ b/src/main/java/com/Lsms/CapitalAndExpenditure/gl/PostingEngine.java
@@ -338,6 +338,15 @@ public class PostingEngine {
     @Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRES_NEW)
     public void reverse(String originalEntryUid, String postedBy, String reason, LocalDate onDate) {
         if (!glConfigService.isPostingEnabled()) return;
+        // Same lock as executePost, keyed on the entry being reversed: two reversals of
+        // one entry at the same moment (reopen + supersede, a double click) would both
+        // pass their callers' "already reversed?" check, which runs outside this
+        // transaction. Checked again here, under the lock, so the second one writes nothing.
+        lockReference(originalEntryUid);
+        if (originalEntryUid != null && journalEntryRepository.existsByReversedEntryUidAndIsDeletedFalse(originalEntryUid)) {
+            log.debug("GL entry {} is already reversed - skipping", originalEntryUid);
+            return;
+        }
         JournalEntry orig = journalEntryRepository.findByUid(originalEntryUid)
                 .orElseThrow(() -> new IllegalStateException("Original entry not found: " + originalEntryUid));
         List<JournalEntryLine> origLines = journalEntryLineRepository.findByJournalEntryUid(originalEntryUid);
